<h2>Why Rajasthan?</h2>
<p class="lead">Few states pack this much into one journey. Heritage is everywhere, and the desert is only the beginning.</p>
<div class="why">
<div><b>Thar Desert</b>Golden dunes around Jaisalmer and Bikaner, camel safaris and nights under the stars.</div>
<div><b>Heritage everywhere</b>Hill forts, palaces, havelis and stepwells in almost every district, six forts on the UNESCO list.</div>
<div><b>Lakes and hills</b>Udaipur’s lakes, the ancient Aravalli range and cool green pockets.</div>
<div><b>Wildlife</b>Tigers at Ranthambore and Sariska, birds, leopards and desert fauna.</div>
<div><b>Art and craft</b>Miniature painting, block printing, blue pottery and folk music.</div>
<div><b>Food and festivals</b>Dal baati churma, laal maas, kachori, and fairs like Pushkar and Desert Festival.</div>
</div>
